ment for the last section.\n\nExisting:\n```\n## Conductor-own-turn drain hook\n\nThe conductor's own turn calls `drain_notices()` from `kit.seat_move_notice` at\nthe start of its turn. That drains the mailbox in FIFO order, removes each\nconsumed file so the same notice is never delivered twice, and the conductor\nemits the drained notices as its own prose in `Bot Chat`. An unreadable mailbox\nraises rather than dropping notices.\n```\n\nReplace with description of prepare_turn/consume_turn and reference to seat-move-turn.md, mention inflight, consume-after-success, session id, state.db maybe. Doesn't hurt to add session details to README too. But D7 reads seat-move-turn.md only. Still, good.\n\nNow, should I modify seat-move-notice.py? Possibly add a `--turn` subcommand? No. Leave untouched. But is there any requirement? The dispatch says editable set includes it. Maybe the existing script's `send_notice` call lacks profile_home/env args; but that's not tested. Actually the existing seat-move-notice.py calls send_notice without profile_home, relying on defaults. Fine.\n\nHmm, but wait: is there a chance the bar's D1 etc. fail because send_notice default profile_home resolution differs? The tests pass profile_home explicitly, so writer uses it. Good.\n\nNow, potential mismatch: the mailbox relative path. Test uses `profile_home / \"runtime\" / \"plumbline-seat-notices\"`. Our module uses same. Good.\n\nLet me also double-check: test D1 after prepare asserts `self.assertFalse(list(_mailbox_dir(...).glob(\"*.json\")))`. Our inflight dir is `mailbox/inflight`, glob non-recursive, so no. Good.\n\nNow think about `_recover_inflight` in D2 second prepare: it moves inflight file back, then `inflight.rmdir()`. Then `mailbox.is_dir()` true. `waiting` includes the recovered file. parse. `inflight.mkdir`. move. Return. Good. But note: after `_recover_inflight` removes inflight dir, then we stage (mkdir). Fine.\n\nBut subtle: `_recover_inflight` calls `inflight.rmdir()` even i