D1 asserts `_inflight_dir(...).glob(\"*.json\")` non-empty after staging. Yes.\n\nNow edge: file ordering for recovery. Recovery order doesn't matter.\n\nNow formatting and \"exactly once\": Let me make sure no duplicate. Also maybe include a header that doesn't contain notice ids.\n\nLet me write the module.\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Stage seat-move notices for one conductor turn.\n\nThe Plumbline mailbox (``runtime/plumbline-seat-notices``) is written by side\nprocesses through ``kit.seat_move_notice``.  The conductor's turn launcher uses\nthis module to hand those notices to the Bot Chat exactly once:\n\n* :func:`prepare_turn` recovers notices left staged by a previous failed turn,\n  drains the mailbox in FIFO order into the ``inflight`` staging directory, and\n  returns the parsed notices plus the context string to announce.\n* :func:`consume_turn` is called only after the turn completes successfully.\n  Until it is called, the notices remain in ``inflight`` and a later\n  :func:`prepare_turn` recovers and re-announces them.\n\nA crash between staging and consumption therefore loses nothing: the notice is\nstill on disk and is announced on the retry.  A clean turn removes the staged\nfiles, so a notice is never announced twice.\n\nEverything here operates inside the given profile home.  The module never\nwrites a Hermes session, never shells out to ``hermes``, and claims no lease.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport pathlib\nfrom typing import Iterable, Mapping\n\n__all__ = [\"prepare_turn\", \"consume_turn\", \"format_context\", \"mailbox_dir\", \"inflight_dir\"]\n\n_MAILBOX_REL = pathlib.Path(\"runtime\") / \"plumbline-seat-notices\"\n_INFLIGHT = \"inflight\"\n_FLAG = \"PLUMBLINE_SEAT_NOTICE\"\n\n\ndef _env_flag(env: Mapping[str,str] | None) -> bool:\n    source = os.environ if env is None else env\n    return str(source.get(_FLAG, \"1\")).strip() != \"0\"\n\n\ndef mailbox_dir(profile_home) -> pathlib.Path:\n    return pathlib.Path(profile_home).expanduser() / _MAILBOX_REL\n\n\ndef inflight_dir(profile_home) -> pathlib.Path:\n    return mailbox_dir(profile_home) / _INFLIGHT\n\n\ndef _order_key(path: pathlib.Path):\n    try:\n        mtime = path.stat().st_mtime_ns\n    except OSError:\n        mtime = 0\n    return (mtime, path.name)\n\n\ndef _load_notice(path):\n    with path.open(\"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n        data = json.load(fh)   # raises JSONDecodeError on corruption\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        raise ValueError(f\"seat notice {path.name!r} is not a JSON object\")\n    return data\n\n\ndef _recover_inflight(mailbox, inflight):\n    if not inflight.is_dir():\n        return\n    staged = sorted(inflight.glob(\"*.json\"), key=_order_key)\n    if staged:\n        mailbox.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        for p in staged:\n            os.replace(p, mailbox / p.name)\n    try:\n        inflight.rmdir()\n    except OSError:\n        pass\n\n\ndef format_context(notices):\n    if not notices:\n        return \"\"\n    lines = [\"Seat-move notices awaiting announcement:\"]\n    for n in notices:\n        direction = n.get(\"direction\", \"?\")\n        seat = n.get(\"seat\", \"?\")\n        job = n.get(\"job_id\", \"?\")\n        notice_id = n.get(\"notice_id\", \"?\")\n        lines.append(f\"- {direction}: seat {seat}, job {job}, notice {notice_id}\")\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n\n\ndef prepare_turn(*, profile_home, env=None):\n    if not _env_flag(env):\n        return [], \"\"\n    mailbox = mailbox_dir(profile_home)\n    inflight = mailbox / _INFLIGHT\n    _recover_inflight(mailbox, inflight)\n    if not mailbox.is_dir():\n        return [], \"\"\n    waiting = sorted(mailbox.glob(\"*.json\"), key=_order_key)\n    if not waiting:\n        return [], \"\"\n    # Parse every notice before staging any of them: a corrupt receipt aborts\n    # the turn with the mailbox untouched.\n    notices = [_load_notice(p) for p in waiting]\n    inflight.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    for p in waiting:\n        os.replace(p, inflight / p.name)\n    return notices, format_context(notices)\n\n\ndef consume_turn(*, profile_home, env=None):\n    if not _env_flag(env):\n        return 0\n    inflight = inflight_dir(profile_home)\n    if not inflight.is_dir():\n        return 0\n    removed = 0\n    for p in inflight.glob(\"*.json\"):\n        try:\n            p.unlink()\n            removed += 1\n        except FileNotFoundError:\n            pass\n    try:\n        inflight.rmdir()\n    except OSError:\n        pass\n    return removed\n```\n\nWait: `_load_notice` uses json.load; corrupt raises JSONDecodeError subclass of ValueError. Test expects (JSONDecodeError, OSError). Good.\n\nBut json.load on non-dict returns and we raise ValueError \u2014 not in expected tuple. Test D6 uses invalid text, so JSONDecodeError. Fine. Could change to json.JSONDecodeError for non-dict to be safe? Not needed.\n\nHmm: `_order_key` calls stat; if file vanished, races. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: mtime ordering when files are created with explicit mtimes? Not.\n\nOne concern: tests import module and call `mod.prepare_turn(profile_home=str(self.profile_home), env=self.env)`. Our signature keyword-only matches (they pass keywords). Good. consume_turn similarly.\n\nNow D1: `notices[0][\"seat\"] == \"plumbline-eval\"`. Our returned dict is the parsed JSON. If send_notice stores `seat` top-level. Likely yes. But what if the JSON structure is like `{\"notice_id\":..., \"payload\": {\"seat\":...}}`? Then test would fail but that's the writer's contract; the bar authors know. They wrote `notices[0][\"direction\"]` in test, implying top-level. Good.\n\nAnother thought: Does send_notice include direction/seat/job at top level? Since test asks for them, yes.\n\nNow, do we need to handle `env` disabled by returning empty but still recover? If disabled, maybe still recover inflight so notices aren't stranded? Not tested. Simpler: no-o